    "knowledge_point": "Stating the Vertex of a Vertical Parabola Given Its Equation in Standard Form",
    "problem": "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=12y?$",
    "worked_solution": "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4(3)y.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=3.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$",
